WEBVTT

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:05.100
Cease your crying, Cinderella.

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:08.460
I'll make sure you can go to the ball.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.640
The fairy godmother waved her wand,

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:15.740
and the pumpkin became a carriage,

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:19.400
and her raggedy old clothes 
turned into a beautiful white dress.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:29.810
Hazuki, find your own story.

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:41.140
<i>Where am I?</i>

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:44.770
Why?

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:46.860
You're finally awake.

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:54.160
Um... I don't know who you are,

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:55.240
but if you could untie me...

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:56.840
I can't do that.

00:00:57.830 --> 00:01:00.150
You've committed a crime.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.430
U-Um... Little girl?

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:06.040
I don't think you 
should play tricks like this.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.250
Arrggh!

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:10.540
That's another crime!

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:12.400
You get the death penalty!

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:13.590
All of a sudden?

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:17.100
In accordance with ancient tradition,

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:18.550
you'll be burned at the stake!

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:20.860
<i>The most cruel execution method of them all!</i>

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:24.100
<i>I really don't think 
tradition is important here!</i>

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:27.310
I'm about to execute your punishment.

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:04.030
<b>Episode 2: 
First Magic</b>

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.080
Wait!

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:11.460
I haven't done anything wrong!

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:14.190
That's what they all say.

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:20.340
You'll be punished 
for treating me like a kid!

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:24.130
No! Help me!

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:25.720
What are you doing?

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:29.140
Mage! Help me! I'm innocent!

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:32.010
At this rate, I'll be wrongly burned
 until I'm crispy on the outside

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:34.060
and slow-roasted on the inside!

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:37.330
Kasumi-san, stop teasing her.

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:39.030
Teasing?

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:48.740
It's the farmer!

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:50.250
The farmer, eh?

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:51.680
I like it.

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:53.660
I started it up as a hobby.

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:56.040
But it means I'm really 
getting into it, I guess.

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:57.500
Here.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:03.760
My book!

00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:06.360
The book before anything else, huh?

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:08.220
You really are interesting.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.410
Welcome.

00:04:12.410 --> 00:04:14.740
I am Sugami, the principal.

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:18.400
I welcome you, Kagimura Hazuki-kun.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:22.390
Welcome to Kuzunoha Girl's Magic Academy!

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:35.510
Did you just say magic academy?

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:38.790
Then are you a magic user?

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:39.940
Yes.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:42.110
A Book User, more specifically.

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:43.920
And you, too?

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:44.680
Yes.

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:48.680
In other words, everyone here uses magic?

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:51.690
<i>The world of magic is real!</i>

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:56.350
If I may add something, so are you.

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:01.190
You were chosen by that 
Original Book of Cinderella.

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:03.400
Original Book of Cinderella?

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:06.330
It contains magical power.

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:08.330
You know what I'm talking about, right?

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:19.380
But all you're doing is letting 
the magic drain out of you now.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:23.540
Uncontrolled power will bring danger 
to you and the people around you.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.280
D-Danger!

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:26.880
It's dangerous...

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:29.520
You have two choices.

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:31.440
The first is to give up your original book,

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:34.850
forget everything, 
and go back to your old world.

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:41.540
The other is to become a student at this school 
and become a proper Book User.

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:43.680
You don't need to decide now.

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:45.530
Take your time.

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:46.570
I'm good at waiting—

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:47.910
I'll do it!

00:05:48.190 --> 00:05:49.660
I'll become a magic user!

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:51.710
Maybe I shouldn't say this,

00:05:51.710 --> 00:05:55.300
but shouldn't you think 
about this a bit more?

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:57.080
I want to be one!

00:05:57.570 --> 00:05:59.290
I'm serious!

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:12.260
Wow...

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:16.470
I'll leave this world connected 
to that library for a while.

00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:19.350
Starting tomorrow, 
please come yourself.

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:34.380
Chant "Maerchen" in front of that bookshelf.

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:35.550
"Maerchen"?

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:38.200
It's a password, you could say,

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:42.210
that opens the door, regardless 
of whether you can use magic.

00:06:42.730 --> 00:06:44.710
Do you have any questions?

00:06:46.390 --> 00:06:48.870
See you tomorrow then, 
Kagimura Hazuki-san.

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:49.680
Um...

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:50.740
Yes?

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:54.000
What's your name?

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:56.440
Call me Tsuchimikado, please.

00:06:56.940 --> 00:07:00.620
Thank you for bringing me my hamburger.

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:26.040
<i>The Original Cinderella...</i>

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:28.630
<i>Kuzunoha Girl's Magic Academy.</i>

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:31.790
<i>And Tsuchimikado-san...</i>

00:07:41.650 --> 00:07:43.230
M-Maerchen!

00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:53.290
<i>Tsuchimikado-san's so pretty.</i>

00:07:54.790 --> 00:07:56.460
<i>Your tie is off center.</i>

00:07:56.460 --> 00:07:58.140
<i>Tsuchimikado-san!</i>

00:08:00.670 --> 00:08:02.370
That's not quite right...

00:08:02.770 --> 00:08:03.720
Do you need something?

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:06.050
Um, well...

00:08:06.050 --> 00:08:08.010
Wh-Where are we going?

00:08:08.010 --> 00:08:09.480
The gym.

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:15.340
You're going to train with the other girls
 who became Maedchen this spring.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:16.740
Maedchen?

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:19.430
Students chosen by the Originals.

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:26.150
This is Kagimura Hazuki, 
who'll be training with you all.

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:29.810
Um, is this really our gym outfit?

00:08:29.810 --> 00:08:31.010
Of course.

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:34.410
It's a traditional outfit for 
Kuzunoha Girl's Magic Academy.

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:36.590
It's traditional, huh?

00:08:37.210 --> 00:08:39.230
I heard she's a person from the other world.

00:08:39.230 --> 00:08:41.120
No way! I've never met one before.

00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:43.330
Silence.

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:49.410
<i>Tsuchimikado-san is really important.</i>

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:51.140
<i>And I'm her friend...</i>

00:08:51.140 --> 00:08:54.710
<i>Wait. I don't even know her first name yet.</i>

00:08:54.710 --> 00:08:56.100
Kagimura-san.

00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:56.930
Yes?

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:00.000
First, I'll show you the basics.

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:10.860
Let your power dwell within me!

00:09:13.210 --> 00:09:14.280
Princess Kaguya!

00:09:32.850 --> 00:09:36.630
This is Bouf Hyure, the basic 
magic spell of an Original User.

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:37.890
Wow!

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:40.940
I thought that since this was an academy 
for magic users, it would be like Harry Potter,

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:42.630
but instead it's a magical girl thing.

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:44.650
Are you the kind that come on TV
 on Sunday mornings,

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:47.870
or the serious battle ones 
that have been popular lately?

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:49.860
She's kind of scary.

00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:51.590
She must be a weird person.

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:53.440
<i>I-I screwed up...</i>

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:56.120
May I continue?

00:09:56.120 --> 00:09:57.050
Of course!

00:09:57.050 --> 00:09:57.990
<i>She's nice!</i>

00:09:57.990 --> 00:10:00.200
<i>Tsuchimikado-san is so nice!</i>

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:04.400
The Bouf Hyure magic unites 
your body with the Original,

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:07.410
making your magic more efficient.

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:10.880
You try it, Kagimura-san.

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:12.460
O-Okay!

00:10:20.230 --> 00:10:20.890
Here I go!

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:29.850
Um...

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:32.400
Is there some kind of 
incantation or something?

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:37.850
The incantation is just 
something to focus your mind.

00:10:37.850 --> 00:10:39.840
So it can be anything?

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:42.880
Don't overthink it.

00:10:42.880 --> 00:10:47.060
Anyone who's made a contract 
with an Original can do it.

00:10:47.060 --> 00:10:49.530
<i>I'll try it like Tsuchimikado-san...</i>

00:10:51.240 --> 00:10:53.540
Trans... form!

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:56.290
Again.

00:10:56.290 --> 00:10:58.390
This time, entrust yourself to the book.

00:10:58.390 --> 00:10:59.090
Okay!

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:13.920
I did it!

00:11:20.270 --> 00:11:22.420
Believe in the book more.

00:11:22.420 --> 00:11:26.330
Your book is Cinderella, 
one of the more powerful ones.

00:11:27.210 --> 00:11:28.690
She said Cinderella!

00:11:28.690 --> 00:11:31.640
Why does <i>she</i> have a book like that?

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:33.380
It must be some kind of mistake.

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:35.840
She doesn't look that special to me.

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:39.630
Can someone from the other 
world even become a Maedchen?

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:41.340
I've never heard that before, either.

00:11:41.730 --> 00:11:45.920
And why is Tsuchimikado-san 
treating her like she's special?

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:48.590
Maybe she's cheating somehow!

00:11:48.590 --> 00:11:50.430
It doesn't make sense!

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:53.090
She's way worse than we are!

00:11:53.090 --> 00:11:56.480
<i>I know this feeling well.</i>

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:57.940
<b>Kagimura</b>

00:11:58.270 --> 00:12:01.360
<i>The first day I transferred 
to the high school in Tokyo,</i>

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:03.490
<i>and I introduced myself...</i>

00:12:05.310 --> 00:12:06.290
<i>It's no good...</i>

00:12:09.380 --> 00:12:10.450
<i>A book...</i>

00:12:10.870 --> 00:12:12.580
<i>I have to read a book...</i>

00:12:12.140 --> 00:12:13.150
Kagimura-san!

00:12:13.300 --> 00:12:14.470
Kagimura-san!

00:12:17.680 --> 00:12:20.960
If you're not feeling well, 
I'll take you to the nurse's office.

00:12:21.620 --> 00:12:23.470
No, I'm fine.

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:24.290
<i>Huh?</i>

00:12:24.790 --> 00:12:26.410
<i>I've calmed down.</i>

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:36.190
<i>Story Syndrome...</i>

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:39.220
<i>Normally, I'd have to read 
a book to calm down.</i>

00:12:40.450 --> 00:12:41.770
Kagimura-san.

00:12:41.770 --> 00:12:43.140
It's okay.

00:12:43.140 --> 00:12:45.740
Take your time with it.

00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:49.350
Tsu-Tsuchimikado-san!

00:12:49.350 --> 00:12:50.330
Yes?

00:12:54.360 --> 00:12:56.090
It's ready.

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:02.150
S-See you tomorrow.

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:14.100
<i>I didn't get to ask her first name...</i>

00:13:21.260 --> 00:13:24.150
Don't you have to tell her?

00:13:25.390 --> 00:13:27.030
About the Hexennacht.

00:13:32.030 --> 00:13:35.960
There's a lot I have to tell her first.

00:13:41.350 --> 00:13:43.550
Today, we'll train with these.

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:48.300
In other words, I'm starting 
over from the baby level?

00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:53.260
I think you're still just not used to magic.

00:13:53.260 --> 00:13:54.850
Not used to it?

00:13:55.420 --> 00:13:59.470
Be honest. Do you think you can use magic?

00:13:59.470 --> 00:14:03.690
Um, I... just don't really think so.

00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:04.660
Right?

00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:08.070
So... First, I want you to use 
these tools for children,

00:14:08.070 --> 00:14:10.950
so you can get more 
experience with magic.

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:17.670
<b>Shizuka</b>

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:19.370
Shizuka?

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:21.550
I-I'm sorry...

00:14:21.550 --> 00:14:25.150
I asked that magical tools 
for children be sent from home.

00:14:25.150 --> 00:14:28.440
And for some reason, 
they sent one of my old toys...

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:33.850
<b>Shizuka</b>

00:14:31.130 --> 00:14:33.850
<i>Her name is Tsuchimikado Shizuka-san.</i>

00:14:34.250 --> 00:14:36.630
Let me have that.

00:14:36.630 --> 00:14:37.360
Please.

00:14:40.070 --> 00:14:41.080
No.

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:42.560
I want this.

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:43.690
I'll use this!

00:14:45.330 --> 00:14:46.340
Is that okay?

00:14:46.340 --> 00:14:48.740
L-Let's get started!

00:14:55.600 --> 00:14:59.140
What's important with magic 
is imagination and concentration.

00:14:59.140 --> 00:15:02.390
But this is a spell 
that even children can use.

00:15:02.390 --> 00:15:04.260
Just relax.

00:15:04.260 --> 00:15:05.380
O-Okay.

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:08.050
<i>Baby level...</i>

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:12.360
<i>But what if I fail at this simple magic, too?</i>

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:14.220
<b>Expulsion</b>

00:15:14.570 --> 00:15:18.650
<i>And then, I'll never 
be able to come here again!</i>

00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:20.440
<i>And...</i>

00:15:20.860 --> 00:15:23.520
<i>Tsuchimikado-san won't like me.</i>

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:26.780
<i>Maybe she'll be disappointed and abandon me.</i>

00:15:28.130 --> 00:15:29.650
<i>I don't want that!</i>

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:37.350
<i>What's important is 
imagination and concentration.</i>

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:41.360
<i>What appears when 
a magic user waves their wand?</i>

00:15:49.290 --> 00:15:50.260
I did it...

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:51.940
A-A pumpkin?

00:15:51.940 --> 00:15:53.470
Why?

00:15:53.750 --> 00:15:54.630
I did it!

00:15:54.630 --> 00:15:56.610
Tsuchimikado-san, I did it!

00:15:56.610 --> 00:15:57.240
Yes.

00:15:57.240 --> 00:15:59.770
Thank you! 
It's thanks to you!

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:02.210
I can use magic, right?

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:04.280
I'm an Original User now, right?

00:16:05.950 --> 00:16:08.500
Congratulations, Kagimura-san.

00:16:09.930 --> 00:16:10.740
Who's there?

00:16:12.580 --> 00:16:14.450
You found me, huh?

00:16:14.840 --> 00:16:16.160
Who's that?

00:16:16.340 --> 00:16:17.160
Hey.

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:19.400
I'm Yumelia Kazan.

00:16:19.400 --> 00:16:22.870
I'm... an exchange student, you could say.

00:16:23.110 --> 00:16:27.130
I heard that you made a contract 
with the Original Cinderella.

00:16:27.140 --> 00:16:28.360
Y-Yeah...

00:16:28.360 --> 00:16:30.600
There's no need to answer her.

00:16:30.600 --> 00:16:32.080
Eventually, you and she will...

00:16:32.080 --> 00:16:32.950
Eventually...

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:35.990
Hey, you still haven't told her?

00:16:35.990 --> 00:16:38.690
The Hexennacht is about to begin.

00:16:38.690 --> 00:16:40.170
Hexennacht?

00:16:40.170 --> 00:16:41.660
A battle between schools,

00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:45.470
where we beginner Original Users
 fight each other for real.

00:16:46.310 --> 00:16:51.700
If you win, you'll get 
a magic that grants any wish.

00:16:51.700 --> 00:16:53.770
W-Wait!

00:16:53.770 --> 00:16:56.350
Th-That's a little too dark 
for a Sunday morning show.

00:16:56.350 --> 00:16:58.320
So, it's a battle show, then?

00:16:59.040 --> 00:17:02.540
Your Cinderella is a book 
with incredible power.

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:06.500
With that power, 
you can win the Hexennacht.

00:17:06.820 --> 00:17:11.950
That's why Shizuka is so desperately 
trying to train you, isn't it?

00:17:11.950 --> 00:17:13.010
Correct.

00:17:19.310 --> 00:17:20.260
I see.

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:23.310
Yeah, it's only natural.

00:17:23.820 --> 00:17:27.920
It's kind of weird that you'd be nice 
to me for no reason when we've just met.

00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:29.400
Normally, you wouldn't do that, right?

00:17:29.770 --> 00:17:32.540
I think I had the wrong idea, maybe.

00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:34.220
I was stupid to get my hopes up...

00:17:34.220 --> 00:17:36.280
Um, Kagimura-san?

00:17:36.650 --> 00:17:37.820
Don't worry.

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:39.870
That's the kind of character I am.

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:43.720
<i>I felt betrayed because 
it wasn't how I thought things were.</i>

00:17:44.170 --> 00:17:45.500
I'll go home for today, okay?

00:17:46.690 --> 00:17:47.750
Kagimura-san?

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:50.880
<i>Thank you! 
It's thanks to you!</i>

00:17:58.760 --> 00:18:00.470
<i>I'm awful, aren't I?</i>

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:03.640
<i>That's why I've never 
made a friend in my life.</i>

00:18:04.320 --> 00:18:06.730
There she goes, huh?

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:08.790
Why aren't you following her?

00:18:09.990 --> 00:18:11.850
P-Principal!

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:19.030
I hurt Kagimura-san.

00:18:19.510 --> 00:18:22.460
I was so focused on trying 
to get what I wanted...

00:18:22.460 --> 00:18:24.390
I didn't think about how she felt, at all.

00:18:24.860 --> 00:18:26.470
Even if that's true,

00:18:26.470 --> 00:18:30.100
without thinking, you reached out 
your hand to try and stop her.

00:18:30.100 --> 00:18:33.670
Isn't that enough of a reason?

00:18:37.690 --> 00:18:39.280
Yumelia Kazan.

00:18:40.170 --> 00:18:42.270
I ordered you to clean the library

00:18:42.270 --> 00:18:45.220
as punishment for the mess 
you made in the school.

00:18:45.220 --> 00:18:48.400
I-I was just about to go!

00:18:55.700 --> 00:18:58.120
Worry all you like.

00:18:58.120 --> 00:19:00.220
That's what students should do.

00:19:05.860 --> 00:19:07.030
Kagimura-san.

00:19:11.890 --> 00:19:13.170
Tsuchimikado-san?

00:19:14.860 --> 00:19:17.510
I-I...

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:20.690
U-Um...

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:30.310
<i>Wh-What is this?</i>

00:19:30.310 --> 00:19:31.850
<i>What's going on here?</i>

00:19:32.610 --> 00:19:36.960
The Tsuchimikado are the 
oldest magic users in Japan.

00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:41.370
My mother was an amazing Original User.

00:19:42.100 --> 00:19:45.170
I heard she fought in the Hexennacht.

00:19:45.170 --> 00:19:47.770
So I want to be like her...

00:19:49.170 --> 00:19:50.120
Kagimura-san!

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:51.620
Yes?

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:54.940
My favorite food is hamburgers.

00:19:56.390 --> 00:19:59.270
I was the only daughter 
of the Tsuchimikados,

00:19:59.270 --> 00:20:02.940
and I was raised very 
strictly since I was young.

00:20:03.600 --> 00:20:07.220
I've never done anything with my mother

00:20:07.220 --> 00:20:09.190
that most people would 
consider familial.

00:20:10.400 --> 00:20:11.310
But...

00:20:12.030 --> 00:20:17.640
Just once, we sat across from each 
other and ate hamburgers like this.

00:20:19.310 --> 00:20:21.530
She was so nice,

00:20:21.980 --> 00:20:23.930
and I was so little,

00:20:23.930 --> 00:20:27.790
that a hamburger felt like 
some kind of special food.

00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:30.330
So I thought if I had a hamburger...

00:20:30.740 --> 00:20:32.010
If I was here...

00:20:32.010 --> 00:20:34.750
I could make up with you.

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:39.090
I'm sorry, Kagimura-san.

00:20:39.820 --> 00:20:41.840
<i>Say something... Say something!</i>

00:20:42.900 --> 00:20:46.300
I-I want you to call me by my 
first name, not my last name!

00:20:49.670 --> 00:20:51.530
If you don't want to, that's fine!

00:20:51.530 --> 00:20:53.690
Really! Don't worry about it!

00:20:53.690 --> 00:20:57.190
Then call me by my first name, too.

00:20:57.940 --> 00:20:58.690
Can I?

00:20:58.920 --> 00:21:02.780
Of course... Hazuki-san.

00:21:02.980 --> 00:21:05.320
Yeah... Shizuka-chan.

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:09.280
It feels strange.

00:21:10.260 --> 00:21:11.490
I agree.

00:21:12.900 --> 00:21:13.700
Kasumi-san!

00:21:13.700 --> 00:21:14.810
When did you get here?

00:21:16.010 --> 00:21:17.880
Call me Ariko-san.

00:21:23.530 --> 00:21:27.900
<i>Mom told me to find my own story.</i>

00:21:28.990 --> 00:21:34.160
<i>Yes... This is when my story began.</i>

00:23:05.730 --> 00:23:06.850
It's time for "What? Why? Maedchen!"

00:23:06.850 --> 00:23:10.120
Our first letter is from 
Kagimura Hazuki-chan in Tokyo!

00:23:10.120 --> 00:23:13.730
Big Sis Ariko, what's an Original Book?

00:23:13.730 --> 00:23:14.540
Google it.

00:23:14.540 --> 00:23:16.340
Next, it's from Princess Shizuka in Kyoto!

00:23:16.340 --> 00:23:19.090
What kind of person do you suppose she is?

00:23:19.090 --> 00:23:21.380
Dear Big Sis Ariko,

00:23:21.380 --> 00:23:23.320
on this splendid day in early spring,

00:23:23.320 --> 00:23:24.950
I hope that you are doing well—

00:23:24.950 --> 00:23:26.050
Too long!

00:23:26.050 --> 00:23:27.400
We're out of time!

00:23:27.400 --> 00:23:30.050
Next time: The Hexennacht Is Here!

00:23:28.470 --> 00:23:35.060
<b>Episode : 
The Hexennacht Is Here!</b>

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:32.940
What's a Hexennacht?

00:23:32.940 --> 00:23:34.070
Google it!

00:23:35.060 --> 00:23:40.050
<b>Illustration: Miyachi</b>
